'''Exalted Weapons''' are special weapons exclusive to certain Warframes that can only be summoned and used upon activating their corresponding Warframe's ability. Exalted Weapons will take the place of the weapon in the corresponding weapon slot when activated (e.g. {{WF|Excalibur}}'s {{A|Exalted Blade}} replacing his melee, {{WF|Hildryn}}'s {{A|Balefire}} replacing her secondary), with the exception of {{WF|Jade}}'s {{A|Glory on High}}, {{WF|Mesa}}'s {{A|Peacemaker}}, {{WF|Titania}}'s {{A|Razorwing}}, and {{WF|Voidrig}}'s {{A|Guard Mode}} which disables all other weapons.

The stats and performances of these weapons are affected by [[mods]] equipped on the weapons themselves and also by certain mods equipped on the Warframe, such as {{Stat|Ability Duration}} mods, depending on the weapon. Certain mods, such as [[Weapon Augments]], cannot be equipped on Exalted Weapons and [[Riven Mods]] are not generated for them. These weapons do not utilize ammunition and instead consume energy (with the exception of {{WF|Cyte-09}}'s {{A|Neutralize}} which uses both), either per shot or continuously, while active. To see which specific mods affect which weapon, visit their ability pages.

All Exalted Weapons come pre-built with an {{Resource|Orokin Catalyst}}, regardless of whether the Warframe has an equipped {{Resource|Orokin Reactor}} or not, and can be [[Polarization|Polarized]] with {{Resource|Forma}}.

